-- The shop's own hookahs and the hoses' photo tag (2026-11-27). Owner: "whatever is ready put it on the site right now so the
-- client can add in the details", "put up the og photos of the hookahs with a 'to be replaced' tag", "put a photo to be
-- changed tag on all the hoses". Two parts, each exactly what `catalog.py seed` writes (store/tools/catalog/test_catalog.py
-- checks they still match). Not applied live yet. Safe to run twice. Needs store/public/img/pc/hookah/ and
-- store/src/img-versions.json deployed with the same commit. Run after shop-photos-2026-11-27.sql and hookah-glass-2026-11-27.sql;
-- never re-run hoses-2026-11-27.sql or shop-photos-2026-11-27.sql after this file: their hose lines would take the tag off
-- again (run this file again after them if that happens).
-- 1. Hoses (store/catalog/suppliers/shop-hoses/master.json): all 31 (OSS-120001 to OSS-120031) get facts_known.photo_label =
--    'replace', so each shows "Photo to be replaced". The photos stay as they are. Over a database where shop-photos-2026-11-27.sql
--    is applied, facts_known is the only column these lines change (every other supplier column is already what they write).
-- 2. Hookahs (store/catalog/suppliers/shop-hookahs/master.json): 27 of the shop's own hookahs, OSS-140001 to OSS-140027: 26 in 21
--    families of their own, plus one colour of the Ace Rose; section Hookahs, Price TBD, in the shop, stock not counted, weight
--    unknown. Names from the hookah council's identification: the maker's full name where exact (Steamulation Mini Gen II,
--    Steamulation Pro X II, Contraband Kingpin, Contraband Scarface), the brand alone where only the brand is readable (MIG,
--    Hookah Monarchy, Performance Smoke, HG), else a plain description; every one is on the back office's Needs info list to
--    rename and check. The four Steamulations (OSS-140001 to OSS-140004) show the maker's or a retailer's photo of that model
--    and colour (photo_src keeps the page); the other 23 show the shop's original photo, full tile, with "Photo to be
--    replaced". The blue Ace Rose (OSS-140027) joins the Ace Rose's family (family 'ace-rose') as one more colour; OSS-100150
--    is not touched.
-- Rollback.
--   Hoses: UPDATE products SET facts_known = json_remove(facts_known, '$.photo_label'), updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ','now')
--            WHERE supplier_id = 'shop-hoses' AND json_valid(facts_known) AND json_extract(facts_known, '$.photo_label') = 'replace';
--   Hookahs: first check nothing has been sold: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM order_items WHERE sku LIKE 'OSS-14____'; if that is not 0,
--   do not delete: UPDATE products SET listed = 0, active = 0 WHERE supplier_id = 'shop-hookahs'. Otherwise (this also drops any
